# The bundle is rebuilt in CI and compared with the committed file byte for byte. The PDB inside
# the bundle stores a checksum of each source file, so the line endings of the .cs files change
# the bytes. This rule gives every checkout the same source bytes, whatever core.autocrlf says on
# the machine. CRLF is the form that a Windows checkout has, and Windows is where the bundle builds.
*.cs text eol=crlf
